Okay, so CountSpatula, the very promising elven female wizard, was
storming through the dungeon.  She had stomped Sokoban and received a
bag of holding, which was immediately blessed, received another bag of
holding as a random in the mines, had not one, but two luckstones
which somehow had also been randomly generated, two magic markers from
a bones file, and (this is the best part), a wand of wishing which was
a Sokoban random, which she used to get blessed +3SDSM (already had a
CoMR).  Strength high from pushing around boulders and eating spinach,
maxed intelligence (no Helm of Brilliance yet), rest of the stats were
pretty damn good.  A 15 charisma made sure items in shops weren't
horribly priced.

Dungeon level 19 was her doom.

Do air elementals only exist on the Plane of Air?  Because I wasn't
there, and that bastard stomped me!  I'm guessing it was a polytrap
mixed with a nefarious gnome.

I'd like, if possible, a bit of help on how to deal with those
creatures.  I didn't have a /oCancellation, nor one of teleport, and I
really don't know how else I might deal with them, other than to
pummel them back.

I described them to a friend as a tornado filled with "I'm going to
stomp you" debris.  Fits.

Her HP was 131, maxed at the time, and it took maybe 5 turns.

So, yeah, YASD.


